senses.gloss:
शतखण्ड a. consisting of a hundred pieces;
 ˚ण्डं
कृ break in a hundred pieces.*

शतजित् a. vanquishing hundreds;
 m. E. of Viṣṇu, a man's
name.

शत॑पत्त्र a. having a hundred feathers or leaves;
 m.
wood-pecker, n. a lotus-flower.

शतपथ a. having a hundred paths, many-sided;
 m. &
˚ब्राह्मण n. T. of a Brāhmaṇa.

शतबुद्धि a. having hundredfold understanding;
 m. N.
of a fish.

शत॑मान a. hundredfold;
 m. n. a weight of a hundred
Mānas in gold or silver.

शतमुख a. having a hundred openings on issues;
 m. N.
of an Asura etc.

शत॑शारद a. containing or granting a hundred autumns
or years;
 n. such a period.

शतशृङ्ग a. having a hundred horns;
 m. N. of a
mountain.

शतह॑न् f. ˚घ्नी॑ killing a hundred;
 f. ˚घ्नी a cert.
weapon.

सत्य॑ a. real, true, genuine;
 serious, valid, effective,
sincere, faithful, honest, good. m. E. of Kṛṣṇa, N. of a genius etc.
f. आ E. of Durgā, N. of a daughter of Dharma etc. n. the real or
true, reality, truth;
 true character, sincerity, faithfulness;
 vow,
promise, oath;
 also adv. really, truly, indeed, yes, very well;
 of
course, it is true (also यत्सत्यम्)—yet (तु, किं तु or तथापि).
Instr. सत्येन according to truth;
 तेन सत्येन (±यथा) as truly
as this, by this truth, on this account or for this reason.

सत्त्व॑ n. being, existence, reality, nature, character;
firmness, resolution, energy, courage;
 goodness (ph.);
 spiritual or
intellectual being, spirit or vital. breath;
 real being, thing, object;
(also m.) living or sentient being, esp. animal, beast;
 phantom,
spectre, imp, goblin.

सतत (adj. ˚—) continual;
 n. & ˚— adv. continually,
incessantly, always, ever;
 w. नं never.

सतत्त्व n. the real or ture nature;
 ˚तस् adv. in
truth, really.

सतो॑बृहन्त् a. equally high or great;
 f. ˚हती N. of
a metre.

सत्कार m. good treatment or service, esp. good reception
of a guest, hospitality;
 burning of a dead body.

सत्क्रिया f. putting in order, preparing;
 also =
सत्कार, i.g. ceremony, festival of (—˚).

साति॑ f. gain, acquisition, wealth, property;
 winning the
prize, making booty.

सत्त्र॑ n. sacrificial session or any meritorious action of
equal worth;
 alms-house, hospital.

सत्रा॑ adv. at once, together;
 along with (instr.);
 at all,
by all means;
 thoroughly, much too.

सत्त्ववन्त् a. having a (strong) character;
 energetic,
resolute, courageous.

सत्त्वशालिन् a. having a (strong) character;
 energetic,
resolute, courageous.

सत्त्वस्थ a. having character or courage;
 adhering to
goodness (ph.).

सत्यवन्त् a. true, veracious;
 m. & f. ˚वती a man's &
woman's name.

सत्यवादि॑न् a. truth-speaking, truthful;
 abstr.
˚वादिता f. & ˚त्व n.

†सत्यसत्वन् m. a true champion;
 adj. having good
champions.

सात्त्विक f. ई relating to or endowed with the quality
of goodness (ph.);
 courageous, energetic, virtuous, brave.

2 सात्वत f. ई relating to the Satvant or Sātvata
(Kṛṣṇa);
 m. a follower of Kṛṣṇa.
